  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0501 and it contains six tables. The first table is Aircraft, which has columns for the affiliated airline, aircraft ID, aircraft model, aircraft status, manufacture date, and maximum passenger capacity. The second table is Crew_Member, which has columns for crew member ID, gender, name, phone, and position. The third table is Passenger, which has columns for gender, identification number, name, passenger ID, and phone. The fourth table is Flight, which has columns for aircraft ID, departure airport, departure time, flight ID, landing airport, landing time, responsible captain ID, and foreign keys for aircraft ID and responsible captain ID. The fifth table is Maintenance_Record, which has columns for aircraft ID, maintenance date, maintenance description, maintenance personnel ID, maintenance type, and foreign keys for aircraft ID and maintenance personnel ID. The sixth table is Ticket_Order, which has columns for booking time, flight ID, passenger ID, seat number, ticket price, and foreign keys for flight ID and passenger ID.",
  "gold_question": "the database is an aircraft information management system, primarily used for managing airlines' aircraft, flights, crew members, maintenance records, and passenger information. the main functions of the system include recording basic aircraft information, flight scheduling, crew allocation, maintenance records; tracking passengers' flight reservations and ticket purchases; providing inquiries into aircraft maintenance history and flight information.\n\nthe system stores basic aircraft information.\nfields: aircraft id, aircraft model, manufacture date, maximum passenger capacity, aircraft status, affiliated airline\nthe system records each aircraft's basic data, such as aircraft model, manufacture date, maximum passenger capacity, current status (e.g., under maintenance, awaiting flight, in-flight), and associates it with the affiliated airline.\n\nthe system stores information of the crew members (including captain, co-pilot, etc.).\nfields: crew member id, name, gender, position, phone\nthe system records crew members' personal information, including name, position, and contact details, facilitating the management of crew members for each flight.\n\nthe system stores basic passenger information.\nfields: passenger id, name, gender, identification number, phone\nthe system records detailed passenger information, such as name, gender, identification number, and contact details, supporting passenger identification management and flight arrangements.\n\nthe system records detailed flight information, including departure and landing times, flight number, etc.\nfields: flight id, aircraft id, responsible captain id, departure airport, landing airport, departure time, landing time\nthis data is used to manage basic flight information, including flight number, departure and landing airports, aircraft id, and flight times, associating the aircraft id with the aircraft table and responsible captain id with the crew member table.\n\nthe system records the maintenance history of aircraft.\nfields: maintenance personnel id, aircraft id, maintenance date, maintenance description, maintenance type\nthis data associates maintenance personnel (crew members) and aircraft, recording maintenance date, maintenance details, etc., to facilitate tracing the maintenance history of aircraft.\n\nthe system records passenger ticket purchase information.\nfields: passenger id, flight id, booking time, seat number, ticket price\nthe system records passenger booking information, including the purchased flight, seat number, ticket price, and booking time, associating passengers with flights.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0501.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0501\nCREATE TABLE `Aircraft` (\n  `aircraft_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `affiliated_airline` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `aircraft_model` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `aircraft_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `manufacture_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `max_passenger_capacity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`aircraft_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Crew_Member` (\n  `crew_member_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`crew_member_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Passenger` (\n  `passenger_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `identification_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`passenger_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Flight` (\n  `flight_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `aircraft_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `departure_airport` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `departure_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `landing_airport` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `landing_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `responsible_captain_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`flight_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`aircraft_id`) REFERENCES `Aircraft` (`aircraft_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `flight_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`responsible_captain_id`) REFERENCES `Crew_Member` (`crew_member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Maintenance_Record` (\n  `maintenance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `aircraft_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_description` text NOT NULL,\n  `maintenance_personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`maintenance_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `maintenance_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`aircraft_id`) REFERENCES `Aircraft` (`aircraft_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `maintenance_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`maintenance_personnel_id`) REFERENCES `Crew_Member` (`crew_member_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Ticket_Order` (\n  `ticket_order_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `booking_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `flight_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `passenger_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `seat_number` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `ticket_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ticket_order_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`flight_id`) REFERENCES `Flight` (`flight_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `ticket_order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`passenger_id`) REFERENCES `Passenger` (`passenger_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
